                "text": "I'm figuring out how the top stalactite shapes relate to the stacked 5-blocks below them, testing whether the top shape extends downward based on how many 5-cells are underneath and converts into 1s.\n\nFor each column group, I'm comparing the depth pattern of the top shape (rows2-3) against the shape of the corresponding 5-block below, checking if they already match or if the top shape needs extra 1-cells added to mirror the 5-block's outline exactly.\n\nGrouping continues: rows6-7 cols10-12 plus row8 col10 plus row9 cols10,11 form one shape, col5 rows8-9 form another, and row8 cols7,8 with row9 col8 form a third.\n\nMatching top C (1 wide, depth 2) against the col5 group works exactly with no additions needed. For top B (cols6,7) against the cols7,8 group, the right column needs depth 2 while the left stays depth 1, so I'd add row3 col7 to make col7 reach depth 2, checking whether mirroring is needed like in training examples.\n\nFor top A (cols1,2,3) matching the big group, I'm mapping the depths: col1 needs depth4 (rows2-5), col2 depth3 with a gap at row4 (rows2,3,5), col3 depth2 (rows2,3). I'm working out which existing 2s need to become 1s across rows2-5 for columns 1-3, plus row2 col12 and the col6,7 row2 additions.",
